      "seed": 1254813292,
      "version": 25,
      "versionNonce": 1717332588,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785175917347,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Features of AWS EC2 ->",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Features of AWS EC2 ->",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ODpzAl3pbjQ6hLmmmbe0l",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1950.6926549789837,
      "y": 5376.648674823278,
      "width": 1045,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGc",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1206579692,
      "version": 316,
      "versionNonce": 316083692,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785176085014,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Provides virtual computing resource.\n2. Computers available are of diff diff configurations(CPU, Storage, RAM etc are configurable).\n3. Provide secure access to the machines(key pair based)\n4. There are pre configured AMI(Amazon machine images) available.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Provides virtual computing resource.\n2. Computers available are of diff diff configurations(CPU, Storage, RAM etc are configurable).\n3. Provide secure access to the machines(key pair based)\n4. There are pre configured AMI(Amazon machine images) available.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FSfEm7vXQmylRExQ7VKFx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1903.1848424789837,
      "y": 5576.394768573278,
      "width": 242,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1917158124,
      "version": 31,
      "versionNonce": 1346344916,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785176110805,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "EC2 Pricing Options ->",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "EC2 Pricing Options ->",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9LJyjyonKmYR81omHnv5N",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1945.4660924789837,
      "y": 5614.527581073278,
      "width": 1133,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bGe",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1549471188,
      "version": 1055,
      "versionNonce": 1640386028,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785176518578,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "we can work on Free tier.\n\nit provides two ways of pricing\n1. On demand -> Here we dont have to pay always a fixed price, it will be dependent on howmuch \n    traffic our EC2 is actually handling.It also depend on what kind of instance we are having\n    suppose we are having a linux instance, then they are going to charge us on second basis, If\nwe are having a windonw instance, then they are going to charge us by the hour based on the usage.\nIf some sesons we have very very low traffic, then this is beneficial.\nIt is also beneficial if we want to move on other cloud later.\n\n\n2. Reserved -> Here there is a contract that happen between us and Amazon, this contract can be 1 year,\n    2 year, it tells us we have to pay this money upfront and then we have this much of bandwidth of\n    each and every resource. prepaid model.\n    If always we are on high traffic, or we know this is the traffic always.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "we can work on Free tier.\n\nit provides two ways of pricing\n1. On demand -> Here we dont have to pay always a fixed price, it will be dependent on howmuch \n    traffic our EC2 is actually handling.It also depend on what kind of instance we are having\n    suppose we are having a linux instance, then they are going to charge us on second basis, If\nwe are having a windonw instance, then they are going to charge us by the hour based on the usage.\nIf some sesons we have very very low traffic, then this is beneficial.\nIt is also beneficial if we want to move on other cloud later.\n\n\n2. Reserved -> Here there is a contract that happen between us and Amazon, this contract can be 1 year,\n    2 year, it tells us we have to pay this money upfront and then we have this much of bandwidth of\n    each and every resource. prepaid model.\n    If always we are on high traffic, or we know this is the traffic always.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
